commit c6999ac3d5f91b438937f2bacfd9a8d224e208c9

C03: a screen reading quotes the recognized text and may not use words it lacks (SCREEN1411)

SCREEN1409 measured the reviewed screen reading with the read composing: four cases exhausted the 5-second composition budget trying to transcribe the whole recognized text, and three published summaries the text never supported (a «Fable limit» warning, generated scripts, an execution flow).

llm._ocr_unsupported_terms / _payload_fact_defect: for a verified ocr.read, every content word of the final (five letters or more, folded, compared by four-letter stem) must appear in the recognized text or in the request, except a framing vocabulary about reading a screen; otherwise ocr_unsupported_terms, with a retry hint that asks to quote two or three lines verbatim and add nothing.
llm.compose_user_message: a verified ocr.read instructs the model to say what the screen shows by quoting two or three recognized lines verbatim and the number of lines, with no purpose, interpretation, warning or full transcription; the default output budget applies (the 512-token allowance of SCREEN1409 is withdrawn).

No .NET change. Offline probe with the real receipt: the invented summaries are vetoed, a quoted report passes, the prompt is 3 K characters. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


